Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Theorem 2 (universal approximation). ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "One hidden layer of \[Sigma] neurons is already enough to approximate any \
continuous function on a cube as closely as wanted, given enough neurons \
(Cybenko [3]; Theorem M2 of [1]). Depth is a matter of efficiency, not of \
possibility."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.98, 0.56, 0.17],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.96, 0.95, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"d4671585-7dc1-4a29-9c14-05c6083ddb48"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. Measuring the error: the loss", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"103065b8-bda5-4452-b7c7-4f776d7dfda3"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "To learn, the network needs a number that says how wrong it is. For M \
examples ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["x", "m"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "350d5ea7-079f-4c87-add4-bc2cf3dc3eb0"],
 " with answers ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["y", "m"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "254d7d49-c4e9-454d-9981-70ccb2e9a717"],
 ", the squared error averages the squared distance between output and answer \
(the factor 1/2 only simplifies the derivative):"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e9e5b9e9-6b84-4f57-8eb5-22f46c6743d3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"L", "=", 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox["1", 
      RowBox[{"2", "M"}]], 
     RowBox[{
      UnderoverscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
       RowBox[{"m", "=", "1"}], "M"], 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"\[DoubleVerticalBar]", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          SuperscriptBox["a", "L"], 
          RowBox[{"(", 
           SubscriptBox["x", "m"], ")"}]}], "-", 
         SubscriptBox["y", "m"]}], "\[DoubleVerticalBar]"}], "2"]}]}]}], "        ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "8", ")"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"792a72f4-05ac-4948-b990-fa07122508e3"],

Cell["\<\
For classification into K classes, the answers are written one-hot: y has a 1 \
in the position of the true class and 0 elsewhere. The output layer uses \
softmax, which turns K numbers into K probabilities, and the loss is the \
cross-entropy, the average of minus the log of the probability given to the \
true class. Softmax outputs are positive and add up to 1:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7d5f1fd0-abca-4ffe-85ba-e93d67e420c4"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["a", "k"], "=", 
    FractionBox[
     SuperscriptBox["e", 
      SubscriptBox["z", "k"]], 
     RowBox[{
      UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", "j"], 
      SuperscriptBox["e", 
       SubscriptBox["z", "j"]]}]]}], "        ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "9", ")"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"035cdf34-5004-43a3-9651-b0ec078244c2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"L", "=", 
    RowBox[{"-", 
     FractionBox["1", "M"], 
     RowBox[{
      UnderoverscriptBox["\[Sum]", 
       RowBox[{"m", "=", "1"}], "M"], 
      RowBox[{
       UnderscriptBox["\[Sum]", "k"], 
       RowBox[{
        SubscriptBox["y", "mk"], " ", 
        RowBox[{"log", " ", 
         SubscriptBox["a", "mk"]}]}]}]}]}]}], "        ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "10", ")"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"9b250fa1-a6fd-47c8-99d3-668c71656680"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["5. Backpropagation: the chain rule, organized", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"9092cc14-0aeb-4848-b197-c15b8af83e78"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Training changes every weight a little in the direction that lowers the \
loss, so it needs the gradient: the derivative of L with respect to every \
entry of every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["W", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "1c872f38-1d68-408e-96bf-ebad858970cf"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["b", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "66903dee-27b6-4e57-880c-6ca21e641bb3"],
 ". Backpropagation [4] computes all of them in one backward sweep, at about \
the cost of one forward pass; textbook accounts are in [5] and [6]."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"a657a8c4-2f21-413c-b337-f8e04355f857"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Theorem 3 (backpropagation). ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Let ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b635a81f-66d0-4926-94c1-8fed3a2b7d9e"],
 " = \[PartialD]L/\[PartialD]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["z", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "ad97d3d4-d3fc-4c3c-97f8-d0ea8afa8581"],
 " be the derivative of the loss with respect to the weighted sums of layer \
l. Then ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "L"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f77732f1-8119-497d-b52b-6c59d4b00c19"],
 " is given by Eq. (11): the first form for a \[Sigma] output with the \
squared error, the second for a softmax output with the cross-entropy and for \
a linear output with the squared error. The earlier ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e50cc427-8c62-4e21-aa9b-88df715200d0"],
 " follow from the backward recursion Eq. (12), and the gradients from Eq. \
(13). Here \[CircleDot] is the Hadamard product: entry-by-entry \
multiplication of two vectors (or matrices) of the same shape: entry i of u \
\[CircleDot] v is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["u", "i"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "b3d5d8a5-9509-40fe-a0bd-6d5e5d05e5a8"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["v", "i"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "f6e98d44-2ed6-4109-8dac-02bd9f6ae75f"],
 "."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.98, 0.56, 0.17],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.96, 0.95, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"487c3e73-fc2d-4620-b506-f5fbb0857edb"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "L"], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox["a", "L"], "-", "y"}], ")"}], "\[CircleDot]", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "\[Prime]",
        MultilineFunction->None], "(", 
       SuperscriptBox["z", "L"], ")"}]}]}], "    ", 
    StyleBox["or",
     FontSlant->"Plain"], "    ", 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "L"], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["a", "L"], "-", "y"}]}]}], "        ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "11", ")"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"8e95d947-bb2f-488f-a9f3-454b400e1b15"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "l"], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      RowBox[{"(", 
       RowBox[{
        SuperscriptBox[
         RowBox[{"(", 
          SuperscriptBox["W", 
           RowBox[{"l", "+", "1"}]], ")"}], "T"], " ", 
        SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", 
         RowBox[{"l", "+", "1"}]]}], ")"}], "\[CircleDot]", 
      RowBox[{
       SuperscriptBox["\[Sigma]", "\[Prime]",
        MultilineFunction->None], "(", 
       SuperscriptBox["z", "l"], ")"}]}]}], 
    RowBox[{",", "    "}], 
    RowBox[{"l", "=", "L", "-", "1", ",", "\[Ellipsis]", ",", "1"}]}], "        ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "12", ")"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"52f3b8c6-a9f0-4872-b41c-62cfe6017bd2"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "L"}], 
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
       SuperscriptBox["W", "l"]}]], "=", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "l"], " ", 
      SuperscriptBox[
       RowBox[{"(", 
        SuperscriptBox["a", 
         RowBox[{"l", "-", "1"}]], ")"}], "T"]}]}], 
    RowBox[{",", "    "}], 
    RowBox[{
     FractionBox[
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "L"}], 
      RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
       SuperscriptBox["b", "l"]}]], "=", 
     SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "l"]}]}], "        ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "13", ")"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"1c5bbceb-2e68-4ce0-ad25-46988b0188d0"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Proof. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "At the output, L depends on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["z", "L"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3c80d0bf-11c9-4e41-9ba3-46346f23220a"],
 " through ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["a", "L"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c429d024-f8e0-4c77-8154-f60c3a6123a4"],
 " = \[Sigma](",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["z", "L"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "16631d9e-0135-4e63-b6b9-ce4b7c86cee6"],
 "), so the chain rule gives (",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["a", "L"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "61daffac-a5b2-4800-821d-85cfd34020dd"],
 " - y) times \[Sigma]\[Prime](",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["z", "L"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "740aeb0e-ccbe-4dd1-bd4a-aec1410bdc2d"],
 ") for the squared error; for softmax with cross-entropy the factors combine \
and leave ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["a", "L"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "be0521d1-1138-4d14-9efe-694c5a62c6cc"],
 " - y. For an earlier layer, ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["z", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "cc49f958-6eee-44be-acc8-015993abe88f"],
 " affects L only through the weighted sums of the next layer, which are W \
\[Sigma](",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["z", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "501287f7-a0ea-4341-b66d-3443764f755b"],
 ") + b with that layer's W and b. Differentiating this composition gives the \
transpose of the next layer's W applied to the next layer's \[Delta], times \
\[Sigma]\[Prime](",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["z", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "48123609-4d60-4271-ab3b-c497dcb8b7dd"],
 ") entrywise, which is Eq. (12). Finally ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["z", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "44e9d998-459d-40ac-9426-f9a433f3eedc"],
 " depends linearly on ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["W", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "0566a97b-e720-4986-8c92-5be597b1a52e"],
 " and ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["b", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "bbfcc787-6fb6-4255-9b53-eded3ddafc1b"],
 ", with coefficients the previous activations and 1, which gives Eq. (13). \
For M samples the gradients are averaged. \:220e"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5a1db5a2-ff18-4b46-952b-d4115fbd9d24"],

Cell["\<\
Read Eq. (12) as Figure M3 read backwards: the error signal \[Delta] flows \
from the output to the input along the same arrows, multiplied by the same \
weights, now transposed.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7fa17d45-19fd-4dfb-9351-484c3f67127f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "The operator \[CircleDot] is the Hadamard product, also called the \
entrywise or Schur product. It multiplies two vectors or matrices of the same \
shape entry by entry, with no sums: entry i of u \[CircleDot] v is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["u", "i"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3fbfdc7e-9d7e-4111-8db1-d8a0cb845a9f"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["v", "i"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7df208f3-57e0-4d31-9342-465a5b7864ab"],
 ", and entry (i, j) of A \[CircleDot] B is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["A", "ij"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "24e66309-b1c7-428b-8c42-cb13eb44edfb"],
 " ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["B", "ij"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "13e02638-bcec-45b7-b6e1-32eebc8d467d"],
 ". For example (1, 2, 3) \[CircleDot] (4, 5, 6) = (4, 10, 18), whereas the \
dot product of the same vectors is the single number 32. In Eq. (12) it \
applies to each neuron its own factor \[Sigma]\[Prime](",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["z", "i"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "16306599-36c8-40ec-961a-a8206f2105c0"],
 "): neuron i passes back only as much error as its \[Sigma] is sensitive at \
its own ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SubscriptBox["z", "i"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "4a8723a4-eb28-46fd-97e7-9950b134ef59"],
 ". In Wolfram Language two lists of the same shape multiplied with a space \
or * are multiplied entrywise, so A (1 - A) and d A (1 - A) in the code are \
exactly \[CircleDot] products."
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e4d82384-1d60-461c-8268-e12683f25717"],

Cell["\<\
Cell c.9 programs Eqs. (6), (8)\[Dash](13) for any number of layers, in the \
row convention of Eq. (5).\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"89d4c701-6a56-4502-996a-aad42ae25582"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.9*)
(* a network is a list of layers {W, b}. In the code the M samples are
   the rows of a matrix, so Eq. (6) z = W a + b becomes Z = A W\:1d40 + b *)
sigma = LogisticSigmoid;
(* softmax row by row; subtracting the row maximum avoids overflow *)
softmax[Z_] := With[{ez = Exp[Z - Max /@ Z]}, ez/Total[ez, {2}]];
(* affine map of a layer, rows = samples: A W\:1d40 + b in every row *)
affine[{W_, b_}, A_] := A . Transpose[W] + ConstantArray[b, Length[A]];
(* forward pass: keep every A^(l); out is the output activation *)
forward[net_, X_, out_] := FoldList[
   Function[{A, l}, If[l == Length[net], out, sigma][affine[net[[l]], A]]],
   X, Range[Length[net]]];
(* three kinds of output: \"mse\" = \[Sigma] output with squared error,
   \"lin\" = linear output with squared error, \"ce\" = softmax output
   with cross-entropy; the losses are Eqs. (8) and (10) *)
loss[\"mse\"][P_, Y_] := Total[(P - Y)^2, 2]/(2 Length[Y]);
loss[\"lin\"][P_, Y_] := loss[\"mse\"][P, Y];
loss[\"ce\"][P_, Y_] := -Total[Y Log[P + 10.^-15], 2]/Length[Y];
outAct = <|\"mse\" -> sigma, \"lin\" -> Identity, \"ce\" -> softmax|>;
(* backpropagation, Theorem 3: the output delta of Eq. (11), then
   Eq. (12) layer by layer, and the gradients of Eq. (13) *)
backprop[net_, X_, Y_, kind_] := Module[{As, L = Length[net], d, g = {}},
   (* forward pass, keeping the activations of every layer *)
   As = forward[net, X, outAct[kind]];
   (* Eq. (11): \[Sigma] output adds the factor \[Sigma]\[Prime]; \"lin\" and \
\"ce\" do not *)
   d = If[kind == \"mse\", (Last[As] - Y) Last[As] (1 - Last[As]),
      Last[As] - Y]/Length[Y];
   (* from the last layer back: gradients of W and b, Eq. (13),
      then \[Delta] of the layer before, Eq. (12) *)
   Do[PrependTo[g, {Transpose[d] . As[[l]], Total[d]}];
    If[l > 1, d = (d . net[[l, 1]]) As[[l]] (1 - As[[l]])],
    {l, L, 1, -1}];
   {loss[kind][Last[As], Y], g}];
(* random start: normal weights with sd 1/\[Sqrt](inputs), zero biases *)
initNet[sizes_] := Table[{RandomReal[NormalDistribution[0,
      1/Sqrt[sizes[[l]]]], {sizes[[l + 1]], sizes[[l]]}],
    ConstantArray[0., sizes[[l + 1]]]}, {l, Length[sizes] - 1}];
\"forward, backprop and initNet defined\"\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"f7a7f8e0-9175-4236-a6ad-82950f82fb83"],

Cell[BoxData["\<\"forward, backprop and initNet defined\"\>"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"64c2c22c-2224-4c81-beb1-bc5b15d12301"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
A backpropagation program can be wrong in ways that still learn a little, so \
it is checked three ways on a small random network: against symbolic \
differentiation with D and against central finite differences of the loss.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6b9f849b-e8d3-4266-8032-2939320a182e"],

Cell["\<\
Table 6. Backpropagation against D and against finite differences.\
\>", "Caption",
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"c7b5afb2-80be-4bc6-bf2e-efa3aed462a1"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.10*)
(* check backprop three ways on a small random 2-3-2 network *)
SeedRandom[4];
netT = initNet[{2, 3, 2}]; XT = RandomReal[{-1, 1}, {5, 2}];
YT = RandomReal[{0, 1}, {5, 2}];
(* the gradients by backprop, Theorem 3 *)
{lossT, gT} = backprop[netT, XT, YT, \"mse\"];
(* 1: automatic differentiation with D on symbolic weights *)
sym = {{Array[wa, {3, 2}], Array[ba, 3]}, {Array[wb, {2, 3}],
    Array[bb, 2]}};
rules = Thread[Flatten[sym] -> Flatten[netT]];
symLoss = loss[\"mse\"][Last@forward[sym, XT, sigma], YT];
(* level -2 holds the symbols wa[i, j], ba[i], ... themselves *)
gD = Map[D[symLoss, #] &, sym, {-2}] /. rules;
(* 2: central finite differences on every weight *)
flat = Flatten[netT]; shape[v_] := Module[{i = 0},
   Map[(i++; v[[i]]) &, netT, {-1}]];
lossAt[v_] := loss[\"mse\"][Last@forward[shape[v], XT, sigma], YT];
gFD = shape@Table[(lossAt[flat + 10.^-6 UnitVector[Length[flat], k]] -
       lossAt[flat - 10.^-6 UnitVector[Length[flat], k]])/(2 10.^-6),
    {k, Length[flat]}];
(* all differences should be at rounding level *)
table[{{\"comparison\", \"largest difference\"},
  {\"backprop vs D\", sci@Max@Abs[Flatten[gT - gD]]},
  {\"backprop vs finite differences\", sci@Max@Abs[Flatten[gT - gFD]]},
  {\"largest gradient entry\", sci@Max@Abs[Flatten[gT]]}}, \"Table 6\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"9ef42a06-922d-4239-8d36-88394f35acd3"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   TagBox[
    GridBox[{{"\"comparison\"", "\"largest difference\""}, {
      "\"backprop vs D\"", 
       TagBox[
        InterpretationBox[
         StyleBox[
          RowBox[{"\"1.4\"", "\[Times]", 
            SuperscriptBox["10", "\"-17\""]}], ShowStringCharacters -> False],
          1.3877787807814457`*^-17, AutoDelete -> True], 
        ScientificForm[#, 2]& ]}, {"\"backprop vs finite differences\"", 
       TagBox[
        InterpretationBox[
         StyleBox[
          RowBox[{"\"1.4\"", "\[Times]", 
            SuperscriptBox["10", "\"-11\""]}], ShowStringCharacters -> False],
          1.406767410894183*^-11, AutoDelete -> True], 
        ScientificForm[#, 2]& ]}, {"\"largest gradient entry\"", 
       TagBox[
        InterpretationBox[
         StyleBox[
          RowBox[{"\"7.2\"", "\[Times]", 
            SuperscriptBox["10", "\"-2\""]}], ShowStringCharacters -> False], 
         0.07203246123622643, AutoDelete -> True], ScientificForm[#, 2]& ]}}, 
     GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Left}}}, AutoDelete -> False, 
     GridBoxBackground -> {
      "Columns" -> {{None}}, "RowsIndexed" -> {1 -> GrayLevel[0.92]}}, 
     GridBoxFrame -> {"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}}, 
     GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
      GridBoxSpacings -> {"Columns" -> {{0.8}}, "Rows" -> {{0.5}}}, 
     BaseStyle -> {FontSize -> 10}], "Grid"], 
   StyleBox["\"Table 6\"", Bold, FontSize -> 11, StripOnInput -> False]},
  "Labeled",
  DisplayFunction->(GridBox[{{
      ItemBox[#2, DefaultBaseStyle -> "LabeledLabel"]}, {
      TagBox[
       ItemBox[
        PaneBox[
         TagBox[#, "SkipImageSizeLevel"], Alignment -> {Center, Baseline}, 
         BaselinePosition -> Baseline], DefaultBaseStyle -> "Labeled"], 
       "SkipImageSizeLevel"]}}, 
    GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Center}}}, 
    AutoDelete -> False, 
    GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
    BaselinePosition -> {2, 1}]& ),
  InterpretationFunction->(RowBox[{"Labeled", "[", 
     RowBox[{#, ",", #2, ",", "Top", ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], "]"}]& )]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"d35ed8ef-\
908b-4c8c-ba54-9cf1d61dcf23"]
}, Open  ]]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["6. Gradient descent: training XOR", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"13ba403b-f1a1-4c60-890e-5afdf95080a0"],

Cell["\<\
Gradient descent repeats one step: compute the gradient by backpropagation \
and move every weight a small distance \[Eta], the learning rate, against it:\
\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"2a614c01-dd77-4b9e-9b8b-8d0a425cf538"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["W", "l"], "\[LeftArrow]", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["W", "l"], "-", 
      RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", 
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "L"}], 
        RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
         SuperscriptBox["W", "l"]}]]}]}]}], 
    RowBox[{",", "    "}], 
    RowBox[{
     SuperscriptBox["b", "l"], "\[LeftArrow]", 
     RowBox[{
      SuperscriptBox["b", "l"], "-", 
      RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", 
       FractionBox[
        RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", "L"}], 
        RowBox[{"\[PartialD]", 
         SuperscriptBox["b", "l"]}]]}]}]}]}], "        ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "14", ")"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"33b3b9c6-fd46-4b76-85dc-4625d52ada7b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.11*)
(* gradient descent, Eq. (14): step every W and b against its gradient;
   keep a snapshot of the network every `every` epochs *)
train[net0_, X_, Y_, kind_, eta_, epochs_, every_] := Module[
   {net = net0, l, g, hist = {}},
   (* each epoch: loss and gradient by backprop, keep a snapshot,
      then the step W \[LeftArrow] W - \[Eta] \[PartialD]L/\[PartialD]W for \
every layer at once *)
   Do[{l, g} = backprop[net, X, Y, kind];
    If[Mod[e - 1, every] == 0, AppendTo[hist, {e - 1, l, net}]];
    net = net - eta g, {e, epochs}];
   AppendTo[hist, {epochs, First@backprop[net, X, Y, kind], net}]];
\"train defined\"\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"479a25fc-0587-455a-aee2-26c9e818db38"],

Cell[BoxData["\<\"train defined\"\>"], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"b1eb92ce-e4e4-45e5-aa77-b0f624d82bd9"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
A 2-3-1 network with random starting weights is trained on the four XOR \
examples, with the squared error and \[Eta] = 4. One pass over the data is an \
epoch.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"e55a1ab7-ee4a-4571-a78e-a26d1b01badf"],

Cell["\<\
Table 7. The loss and the four outputs during training. The network first \
drifts to 0.5 everywhere, the single-neuron answer of Table 4, then breaks \
the symmetry around epoch 300 and settles on XOR.\
\>", "Caption",
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"848ca0ef-779d-4da6-a97f-fb8ef57ce861"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.12*)
(* train a 2-3-1 network on XOR from random weights *)
SeedRandom[7];
xorX = N[inputs]; xorT = List /@ N[xorY];
(* \[Eta] = 4, 3000 epochs, a snapshot every 25 epochs *)
histX = train[initNet[{2, 3, 1}], xorX, xorT, \"mse\", 4., 3000, 25];
(* the loss and the four outputs at a few snapshots *)
table[Prepend[Table[With[{h = histX[[k]]}, {h[[1]], sci[h[[2]]],
      Sequence @@ (NumberForm[#, 3] & /@
         Flatten@Last@forward[h[[3]], xorX, sigma])}],
    {k, {1, 5, 9, 13, 21, 41, 81, Length[histX]}}],
  {\"epoch\", \"loss\", \"out (0,0)\", \"out (0,1)\", \"out (1,0)\",
   \"out (1,1)\"}], \"Table 7\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"1a6ea13e-fb6b-496a-9e7d-4f0e036eef31"],

