Cell["\<\
Backpropagation is matrix algebra too. With the examples as rows, the \
\[Delta] of a layer is an M \[Times] (neurons) matrix, the gradient of W is \
\[Delta]\:1d40 times the activations of the layer before, and the \[Delta] of \
the layer before is \[Delta] W, multiplied entrywise by \[Sigma]\[Prime], \
Eqs. (11)\[Dash](13) in the row convention. Here are all of these matrices \
for the first step of the training of Table 7.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"eb96604d-a9e9-426e-b4b7-a9c339565dc5"],

Cell["\<\
Table 7b. One backward pass of the 2-3-1 network at epoch 0, for the 4 XOR \
examples. The last line checks that the matrix formulas give exactly the \
gradient computed by backprop in cell c.9.\
\>", "Caption",
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"3a867a9f-56af-43ca-b456-12eca78fa2a7"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.12c*)
(* backpropagation in matrices, on the first training step of Table 7:
   the 2-3-1 network at epoch 0, all 4 XOR examples. Rows are
   examples, so every \[Delta] is 4 \[Times] (neurons of its layer) *)
net0 = histX[[1, 3]];
{A0, A1, A2} = forward[net0, xorX, sigma];
d2 = (A2 - xorT) A2 (1 - A2)/4;              (* Eq. (11), 4\[Times]1 *)
gW2 = Transpose[d2] . A1; gb2 = Total[d2];   (* Eq. (13) *)
d1 = (d2 . net0[[2, 1]]) A1 (1 - A1);        (* Eq. (12), 4\[Times]3 *)
gW1 = Transpose[d1] . A0; gb1 = Total[d1];
table[{{\"quantity\", \"size\", \"value\"},
   {\"output \[Delta] = (a - y) \[CircleDot] a \[CircleDot] (1 - a)/M\", \"4\
\[Times]1\", mat[d2]},
   {\"\[PartialD]L/\[PartialD]W (output) = \[Delta]\:1d40 A (hidden)\", \"1\
\[Times]3\", mat[gW2]},
   {\"hidden \[Delta] = (\[Delta] W) \[CircleDot] A \[CircleDot] (1 - A)\", \
\"4\[Times]3\", mat[d1]},
   {\"\[PartialD]L/\[PartialD]W (hidden) = \[Delta]\:1d40 X\", \
\"3\[Times]2\", mat[gW1]},
   {\"\[PartialD]L/\[PartialD]b (hidden) = column sums of \[Delta]\", \"3\", \
col[gb1]},
   {\"same as backprop of c.9?\", \"\",
    gW1 == backprop[net0, xorX, xorT, \"mse\"][[2, 1, 1]]}},
 \"Table 7b. One backward pass in matrix form\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"1b6b3651-4a93-4302-a166-51b8dc7c66d6"],

