Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["8. Balancing a stick on a moving cart", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"a41bf1f6-c74b-4c1b-a47d-d8cd9180480e"],

Cell["\<\
Balance a broom upright on the palm of your hand: you keep it up by moving \
your hand under it, a little ahead of where it falls. The cart-pole is the \
same problem on a rail: a stick of length 1 m (mass 0.1 kg) stands on a hinge \
on a cart (1 kg), and the only control is a horizontal force u on the cart, \
at most 10 N either way. The state is s = (x, v, \[Theta], \[Omega]): cart \
position and speed, the angle of the stick from upright and its angular \
speed. Newton's laws give [7], with g = 9.81 m/s\.b2 and l = 0.5 m the half \
length of the stick,\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b10d8c49-3f4a-4fdf-bbcf-a2734655a0cc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         FractionBox[
          RowBox[{"d", "\[Omega]"}], 
          RowBox[{"d", "t"}]], "=", 
         FractionBox[
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"g", " ", 
            RowBox[{"sin", " ", "\[Theta]"}]}], "-", 
           RowBox[{
            RowBox[{"cos", " ", "\[Theta]"}], " ", "f"}]}], 
          RowBox[{"l", " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             FractionBox["4", "3"], "-", 
             FractionBox[
              RowBox[{
               SubscriptBox["m", "p"], " ", 
               SuperscriptBox["cos", "2"], " ", "\[Theta]"}], 
              RowBox[{
               SubscriptBox["m", "c"], "+", 
               SubscriptBox["m", "p"]}]]}], ")"}]}]]}], 
        RowBox[{",", "    "}], 
        RowBox[{
         FractionBox[
          RowBox[{"d", "\[Theta]"}], 
          RowBox[{"d", "t"}]], "=", "\[Omega]"}]}],
       ScriptLevel->0]},
     {
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"f", "=", 
         FractionBox[
          RowBox[{"u", "+", 
           RowBox[{
            SubscriptBox["m", "p"], " ", "l", " ", 
            SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], " ", 
            RowBox[{"sin", " ", "\[Theta]"}]}]}], 
          RowBox[{
           SubscriptBox["m", "c"], "+", 
           SubscriptBox["m", "p"]}]]}], 
        RowBox[{",", "    "}], 
        RowBox[{
         FractionBox[
          RowBox[{"d", "v"}], 
          RowBox[{"d", "t"}]], "=", 
         RowBox[{"f", "-", 
          FractionBox[
           RowBox[{
            SubscriptBox["m", "p"], " ", "l", " ", 
            FractionBox[
             RowBox[{"d", "\[Omega]"}], 
             RowBox[{"d", "t"}]], " ", 
            RowBox[{"cos", " ", "\[Theta]"}]}], 
           RowBox[{
            SubscriptBox["m", "c"], "+", 
            SubscriptBox["m", "p"]}]]}]}], 
        RowBox[{",", "    "}], 
        RowBox[{
         FractionBox[
          RowBox[{"d", "x"}], 
          RowBox[{"d", "t"}]], "=", "v"}]}],
       ScriptLevel->0]}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1}}, "Rows" -> {{0.8}}}], "        ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "16", ")"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"84d0b836-d7a6-43c6-814f-85c4fb738a0b"],

Cell["\<\
Upright is an equilibrium, but an unstable one: left alone, a 17\[Degree] \
tilt becomes a fallen stick in under a second. It is a classic test of \
control and of learning, because the controller must act continuously and \
every mistake grows.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"79fe32c7-6736-4e56-94b2-81ce891b930b"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["A teacher and a student", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"9530d5fa-0cbc-4edf-850c-de268651ac59"],

Cell["\<\
Control theory gives a good balancing rule. Near upright the equations are \
nearly linear, and for linear equations the LQR (linear quadratic regulator) \
finds the gains K of the best linear rule u = -K\[CenterDot]s; \
LQRegulatorGains computes them. A real motor has a limited force, so the \
teacher saturates smoothly at 10 N:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3cd2a705-38c9-4d53-b1f8-45586d661fc0"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"u", "=", 
     RowBox[{
      SubscriptBox["u", "max"], " ", 
      RowBox[{"tanh", 
       RowBox[{"(", 
        RowBox[{"-", 
         FractionBox[
          RowBox[{"K", "\[CenterDot]", "s"}], 
          SubscriptBox["u", "max"]]}], ")"}]}]}]}], 
    RowBox[{",", "    "}], 
    RowBox[{"s", "=", 
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{"x", ",", "v", ",", "\[Theta]", ",", "\[Omega]"}], ")"}]}], 
    RowBox[{",", "    "}], 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["u", "max"], "=", 
     RowBox[{"10", " ", "N"}]}]}], "        ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "17", ")"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"0a44b5ec-af90-4761-be22-67156c7f2ef1"],

Cell["\<\
The teacher is a nonlinear function of four inputs, exactly the kind of \
function a network with one hidden layer can learn (Theorem 2). The student \
is a 4-8-1 network with \[Sigma] hidden neurons and a linear output, trained \
with the squared error on 3000 random states, each labelled with the force \
the teacher would apply. This is called imitation learning; Widrow and Smith \
[8] trained an early network to balance a broom this way in 1964.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"9c7f7028-7bf1-4001-8385-ba9ea4a0fa24"],

Cell["\<\
Table 10. Four of the 3000 training examples, and the LQR gains of the \
teacher.\
\>", "Caption",
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"e68ec84b-f391-41a4-9415-91139c7a5fa9"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.18*)
(* the cart-pole: a stick of length 1 m on a cart that can be pushed
   left or right. State s = {x, v, \[Theta], \[Omega]}: cart position and \
speed,
   stick angle from upright and its angular speed *)
{g0, mc, mp, len} = {9.81, 1., 0.1, 0.5};  (* len = half stick length *)
rhs[{x_, v_, th_, om_}, u_] := Module[{s = Sin[th], c = Cos[th], f, al},
   f = (u + mp len om^2 s)/(mc + mp);
   al = (g0 s - c f)/(len (4/3 - mp c^2/(mc + mp)));
   {v, f - mp len al c/(mc + mp), om, al}];
(* the teacher: an LQR controller for the straightened (linear)
   equations, with the motor limited to |u| <= 10 N *)
jac = D[rhs[{x, v, th, om}, u], {{x, v, th, om, u}}] /.
   Thread[{x, v, th, om, u} -> 0];
K = First@LQRegulatorGains[StateSpaceModel[{jac[[All, 1 ;; 4]],
      jac[[All, {5}]]}], {DiagonalMatrix[{1, 1, 10, 1}], {{0.1}}}];
umax = 10.;
teacher[s_] := umax Tanh[-K . s/umax];
(* 3000 random states as examples; inputs and targets scaled to ~1 *)
scale = {1., 2., 0.5, 2.};
SeedRandom[3];
states = RandomReal[{-1, 1}, {3000, 4}] . DiagonalMatrix[scale];
cpX = (#/scale) & /@ states;
cpY = List /@ (teacher /@ states/umax);
table[Join[{{\"state {x, v, \[Theta], \[Omega]}\", \"teacher force u (N)\"}},
   Table[{NumberForm[states[[k]], 2], NumberForm[teacher[states[[k]]],
      3]}, {k, 4}], {{\"LQR gains K\", NumberForm[K, 3]}}], \"Table 10\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"add25732-440d-4b65-849c-9c9119888161"],

