Cell["\<\
The network is never shown a moving cart: it only learns a function from \
states to forces. The test is to put it in control. The cart starts at rest \
with the stick tilted 17\[Degree], and the equations (16) are integrated with \
the Runge-Kutta method, step 0.02 s, with the force chosen by the network at \
every step.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3e3df221-7513-407e-a791-a3883a4d5e1b"],

Cell["\<\
Table 11. The loss during training, and what happens when the network at that \
epoch drives the cart. Each epoch it holds the stick a little longer, and \
from about epoch 100 it balances.\
\>", "Caption",
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"bf813876-eef3-406b-964b-9687ef5aaf64"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.19*)
(* a 4-8-1 network imitates the teacher: \[Sigma] hidden layer, linear
   output, squared error (\"lin\"). Then the network alone drives the
   cart and we see whether the stick stays up *)
SeedRandom[5];
histC = train[initNet[{4, 8, 1}], cpX, cpY, \"lin\", 0.5, 4000, 10];
ctrl[net_][s_] := Clip[umax First@First@Last@forward[net, {s/scale},
       Identity], {-umax, umax}];
dt = 0.02;
rk4[f_][s_] := Module[{u = f[s], k1, k2, k3, k4},
   k1 = rhs[s, u]; k2 = rhs[s + dt/2 k1, u];
   k3 = rhs[s + dt/2 k2, u]; k4 = rhs[s + dt k3, u];
   s + dt/6 (k1 + 2 k2 + 2 k3 + k4)];
fallen[s_] := Abs[s[[3]]] > Pi/2;
(* 6 s of motion from a 17\[Degree] tilt; a fallen stick stays fallen *)
s0 = {0., 0., 0.3, 0.};
sim[f_, s1_, n_] := NestList[If[fallen[#], #, rk4[f][#]] &, s1, n];
fate[tr_] := With[{p = FirstPosition[fallen /@ tr, True]},
   If[MissingQ[p], \"balances\", Row[{\"falls at t = \",
      NumberForm[dt (p[[1]] - 1), 2], \" s\"}]]];
table[Prepend[Table[With[{h = histC[[k]]}, {h[[1]],
      NumberForm[h[[2]], 3], fate@sim[ctrl[h[[3]]], s0, 300]}],
    {k, {1, 3, 5, 11, 21, 101, Length[histC]}}],
  {\"epoch\", \"loss\", \"the stick, network in control\"}], \"Table 11\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"2fad1c09-b08f-4da9-acfd-2d9039ee4da9"],

