Cell["\<\
A controller is only useful if it copes with the unexpected. The trained \
network is started almost upright, and the stick is hit twice, at t = 1.5 s \
and at t = 4 s, as if flicked with a finger. Nothing like this was in the \
training data, yet the network runs the cart under the stick and recovers \
each time.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3704e0cf-e85f-424b-b952-5fac3d37675f"],

Cell["\<\
Figure 8. The trained network against two pushes. Press play.\
\>", "Caption",
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"e7b353af-487a-427d-821f-6f530a552a70"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.21*)
(* the trained network against pushes it never saw in training: at
   t = 1.5 s and t = 4 s the stick is hit (\[Omega] jumps by \[PlusMinus]2 \
rad/s) *)
netC = histC[[-1, 3]];
(* the pushes: \[Omega] changes by +2 rad/s at step 75, -2 at step 200 *)
push[k_][s_] := s + Which[k == 75, {0, 0, 0, 2.}, k == 200,
    {0, 0, 0, -2.}, True, 0];
(* each step: the network chooses u, Runge-Kutta moves the
   cart-pole by dt, then a push may hit *)
trajP = FoldList[push[#2][rk4[ctrl[netC]][#1]] &, {0., 0., 0.05, 0.},
   Range[350]];
pushFrames = Table[Show[cartPole[trajP[[n]], ctrl[netC][trajP[[n]]]],
    PlotLabel -> Row[{\"t = \", NumberForm[dt (n - 1), {2, 2}], \" s\",
       If[75 <= n <= 85 || 200 <= n <= 210, \"   push!\", \"\"]}],
    LabelStyle -> figStyle], {n, 1, 351, 2}];
ListAnimate[pushFrames, AnimationRate -> 25,
 AnimationRepetitions -> Infinity,
 AnimationRunning -> False]  (* starts only when play is pressed *)\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"62dc769f-1f3f-43f0-8f9d-5402e585d64a"],

