Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["9. A network learns the physics of a pendulum", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"bedee70f-2737-4545-9308-197745f46e18"],

Cell["\<\
The cart-pole network learned what to do. A network can also learn how a \
system behaves: a model of its dynamics, which can then be run forward in \
time like a simulator. Take a pendulum of length 1 m, with time measured so \
that g/l = 1. Its angle obeys \[Theta]\[DoublePrime] = a(\[Theta]), and we \
pretend not to know the force law a(\[Theta]) = -sin \[Theta]: we only have \
200 measurements of angle and acceleration, with a little noise. A 1-6-1 \
network learns a(\[Theta]) from them, and the learned pendulum is then run by \
itself:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7fa16845-364a-41b4-8907-e0bbaf654ab1"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{
         FractionBox[
          RowBox[{"d", "\[Theta]"}], 
          RowBox[{"d", "t"}]], "=", "\[Omega]"}], 
        RowBox[{",", "    "}], 
        RowBox[{
         FractionBox[
          RowBox[{"d", "\[Omega]"}], 
          RowBox[{"d", "t"}]], "=", 
         RowBox[{"a", "(", "\[Theta]", ")"}]}]}],
       ScriptLevel->0]},
     {
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"E", "=", 
         RowBox[{
          FractionBox[
           SuperscriptBox["\[Omega]", "2"], "2"], "+", 
          RowBox[{"V", "(", "\[Theta]", ")"}]}]}], 
        RowBox[{",", "    "}], 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{
          SuperscriptBox["V", "\[Prime]",
           MultilineFunction->None], "(", "\[Theta]", ")"}], "=", 
         RowBox[{"-", 
          RowBox[{"a", "(", "\[Theta]", ")"}]}]}], "    ", "\[Implies]", 
        "    ", 
        RowBox[{
         FractionBox[
          RowBox[{"d", "E"}], 
          RowBox[{"d", "t"}]], "=", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{"\[Omega]", " ", 
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{
             RowBox[{"a", "(", "\[Theta]", ")"}], "+", 
             RowBox[{
              SuperscriptBox["V", "\[Prime]",
               MultilineFunction->None], "(", "\[Theta]", ")"}]}], ")"}]}], "=",
           "0"}]}]}],
       ScriptLevel->0]}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1}}, "Rows" -> {{0.8}}}], "        ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "18", ")"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"897ff028-8465-4ead-8f01-d4d5d5cb55eb"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Theorem 4 (a learned force law conserves energy). ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "If the model of the acceleration depends on the angle only, \[Theta]\
\[DoublePrime] = a(\[Theta]) with any continuous a, then E = \[Omega]\.b2/2 + \
V(\[Theta]), with V any antiderivative of -a, stays constant along every \
motion. In particular the learned pendulum can never run down or speed up."
}], "Text",
 CellFrame->{{2, 0}, {0, 0}},
 CellFrameColor->RGBColor[0.98, 0.56, 0.17],
 Background->RGBColor[
  0.96, 0.95, 0.92],ExpressionUUID->"7b8866c9-510c-4a52-8e37-6ab40000bdc1"],

Cell[TextData[{
 StyleBox["Proof. ",
  FontWeight->"Bold"],
 "Along a motion, dE/dt = \[Omega] \[Omega]\[Prime] + V\[Prime](\[Theta]) \
\[Theta]\[Prime] = \[Omega] a(\[Theta]) - a(\[Theta]) \[Omega] = 0, because \
\[Theta]\[Prime] = \[Omega] and \[Omega]\[Prime] = a(\[Theta]), as written in \
the second line of Eq. (18). \:220e"
}], "Text",ExpressionUUID->"ef48c851-4b9e-473f-aea6-79946c96a412"],

Cell["\<\
This is a lesson about building models: the right inputs give the right \
structure. A network fed (\[Theta], \[Omega]) could learn a small fake \
friction or push and slowly drift away; one fed \[Theta] alone cannot, \
whatever its weights. To keep this property in the computer, the motion is \
integrated with the leapfrog (velocity Verlet) method [9], which nearly \
conserves energy over very long times, with step 0.05 s.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"637f831c-d5b0-4907-8098-aa545c9d58b7"],

Cell["\<\
The network is trained with Adam, a refinement of gradient descent (Kingma \
and Ba [10]) that keeps a running average m of each gradient entry g and a \
running average v of its square, and divides the step by the square root of \
v; the hats correct the averages for their start at 0, k being the step \
number. Every weight then gets its own step size; the gradients still come \
from backpropagation, Theorem 3:\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"eb052689-92fc-499b-8992-3abd2560d977"],

Cell[BoxData[
 FormBox[
  RowBox[{GridBox[{
     {
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"m", "\[LeftArrow]", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", "1"], " ", "m"}], "+", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"1", "-", 
             SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", "1"]}], ")"}], " ", "g"}]}]}], 
        RowBox[{",", "    "}], 
        RowBox[{"v", "\[LeftArrow]", 
         RowBox[{
          RowBox[{
           SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", "2"], " ", "v"}], "+", 
          RowBox[{
           RowBox[{"(", 
            RowBox[{"1", "-", 
             SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", "2"]}], ")"}], " ", 
           SuperscriptBox["g", "2"]}]}]}]}],
       ScriptLevel->0]},
     {
      StyleBox[
       RowBox[{
        RowBox[{"W", "\[LeftArrow]", 
         RowBox[{"W", "-", 
          RowBox[{"\[Eta]", " ", 
           FractionBox[
            OverscriptBox["m", "^"], 
            RowBox[{
             SqrtBox[
              OverscriptBox["v", "^"]], "+", "\[Epsilon]"}]]}]}]}], 
        RowBox[{",", "    "}], 
        RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox["m", "^"], "=", 
         FractionBox["m", 
          RowBox[{"1", "-", 
           SuperscriptBox[
            SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", "1"], "k"]}]]}], 
        RowBox[{",", "  "}], 
        RowBox[{
         OverscriptBox["v", "^"], "=", 
         FractionBox["v", 
          RowBox[{"1", "-", 
           SuperscriptBox[
            SubscriptBox["\[Beta]", "2"], "k"]}]]}]}],
       ScriptLevel->0]}
    },
    GridBoxAlignment->{"Columns" -> {{Left}}},
    GridBoxSpacings->{"Columns" -> {{1}}, "Rows" -> {{0.8}}}], "        ", 
   StyleBox[
    RowBox[{"(", "19", ")"}],
    FontSlant->"Plain"]}], TraditionalForm]], "DisplayFormula",ExpressionUUID->\
"486b3896-81ed-4f69-90f8-0b3b01925d17"],

Cell["\<\
The pendulum is released at 115\[Degree], far beyond the small-angle range. \
There the true period, 8.35 s, is a third longer than the 2\[Pi] = 6.28 s of \
the textbook law a = -\[Theta] (Hooke's law), so learning the curve, not a \
straight line, is what gets the swing right.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"12f6e280-dcbc-4a23-b338-0a12aaf84f41"],

Cell["\<\
Table 12. The period of the learned pendulum during training. The untrained \
model sends the pendulum over the top; then the period approaches the true \
value, which the linear law misses by 2 s.\
\>", "Caption",
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"3d1f5805-2e99-4541-8ae1-cf01949fc188"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.22*)
(* a pendulum, \[Theta]'' = a(\[Theta]), whose force law a(\[Theta]) = -sin \
\[Theta] we pretend not
   to know: we only have 200 noisy measurements of angle and
   acceleration. A 1-6-1 network learns a(\[Theta]) *)
SeedRandom[11];
thD = RandomReal[{-2.6, 2.6}, 200];
aD = -Sin[thD] + RandomReal[NormalDistribution[0, 0.02], 200];
(* Adam (Kingma and Ba): gradient descent with a running average of
   the gradient (m) and of its square (v), so each weight gets its own
   step size. The gradients still come from backprop of c.9 *)
trainAdam[net0_, X_, Y_, kind_, eta_, epochs_, every_] := Module[
   {net = net0, m = 0 net0, v = 0 net0, l, g, hist = {},
    b1 = 0.9, b2 = 0.999},
   Do[{l, g} = backprop[net, X, Y, kind];
    If[Mod[e - 1, every] == 0, AppendTo[hist, {e - 1, l, net}]];
    m = b1 m + (1 - b1) g; v = b2 v + (1 - b2) g^2;
    net = net - eta (m/(1 - b1^e))/(Sqrt[v/(1 - b2^e)] + 10.^-8),
    {e, epochs}];
   AppendTo[hist, {epochs, First@backprop[net, X, Y, kind], net}]];
SeedRandom[1];
histP = trainAdam[initNet[{1, 6, 1}], List /@ (thD/2), List /@ aD,
   \"lin\", 0.03, 2000, 10];
accel[net_][th_] := First@First@Last@forward[net, {{th/2}}, Identity];
(* run the model: the leapfrog (velocity Verlet) step, 0.05 s *)
h = 0.05;
leap[a_][{th_, om_}] := Module[{o = om + h/2 a[th], t},
   t = th + h o; {t, o + h/2 a[t]}];
p0 = {2., 0.};                      (* released at 115\[Degree] *)
period[tr_] := With[{z = Flatten@Position[Partition[
        Sign[tr[[All, 1]]], 2, 1], {1, -1}]},
   If[Length[z] > 1, NumberForm[h Mean@Differences[z], 3],
    \"goes over the top\"]];
truthP = NestList[leap[-Sin[#] &], p0, 800];
table[Join[{{\"model of the force\", \"loss\", \"period (s)\"}},
   Table[{Row[{\"network, epoch \", histP[[k, 1]]}],
     NumberForm[histP[[k, 2]], 3],
     period@NestList[leap[accel[histP[[k, 3]]]], p0, 800]},
    {k, {1, 3, 6, 11, 51, Length[histP]}}],
   {{\"Hooke's law a = -\[Theta]\", \"\", period@NestList[leap[-# &], p0, \
800]},
    {\"true pendulum a = -sin \[Theta]\", \"\", period[truthP]}}], \"Table 12\
\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"ba3032f9-b241-4d53-abee-2261ac2ba43c"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TemplateBox[{
   TagBox[
    GridBox[{{"\"model of the force\"", "\"loss\"", "\"period (s)\""}, {
       TemplateBox[{"\"network, epoch \"", "0"}, "RowDefault"], 
       TagBox[
        InterpretationBox[
         StyleBox["\"0.327\"", ShowStringCharacters -> False], 
         0.3268048200431531, AutoDelete -> True], NumberForm[#, 3]& ], 
       "\"goes over the top\""}, {
       TemplateBox[{"\"network, epoch \"", "20"}, "RowDefault"], 
       TagBox[
        InterpretationBox[
         StyleBox["\"0.0721\"", ShowStringCharacters -> False], 
         0.0721390100166255, AutoDelete -> True], NumberForm[#, 3]& ], 
       TagBox[
        InterpretationBox[
         StyleBox["\"11.6\"", ShowStringCharacters -> False], 
         11.566666666666668`, AutoDelete -> True], NumberForm[#, 3]& ]}, {
       TemplateBox[{"\"network, epoch \"", "50"}, "RowDefault"], 
       TagBox[
        InterpretationBox[
         StyleBox["\"0.0308\"", ShowStringCharacters -> False], 
         0.030830987273640035`, AutoDelete -> True], NumberForm[#, 3]& ], 
       TagBox[
        InterpretationBox[
         StyleBox["\"8.64\"", ShowStringCharacters -> False], 
         8.637500000000001, AutoDelete -> True], NumberForm[#, 3]& ]}, {
       TemplateBox[{"\"network, epoch \"", "100"}, "RowDefault"], 
       TagBox[
        InterpretationBox[
         StyleBox["\"0.0239\"", ShowStringCharacters -> False], 
         0.023915494267383108`, AutoDelete -> True], NumberForm[#, 3]& ], 
       TagBox[
        InterpretationBox[
         StyleBox["\"8.84\"", ShowStringCharacters -> False], 8.8375, 
         AutoDelete -> True], NumberForm[#, 3]& ]}, {
       TemplateBox[{"\"network, epoch \"", "500"}, "RowDefault"], 
       TagBox[
        InterpretationBox[
         StyleBox["\"0.00391\"", ShowStringCharacters -> False], 
         0.0039051919937127546`, AutoDelete -> True], NumberForm[#, 3]& ], 
       TagBox[
        InterpretationBox[
         StyleBox["\"8.66\"", ShowStringCharacters -> False], 8.6625, 
         AutoDelete -> True], NumberForm[#, 3]& ]}, {
       TemplateBox[{"\"network, epoch \"", "2000"}, "RowDefault"], 
       TagBox[
        InterpretationBox[
         StyleBox["\"0.000213\"", ShowStringCharacters -> False], 
         0.0002133879557099051, AutoDelete -> True], NumberForm[#, 3]& ], 
       TagBox[
        InterpretationBox[
         StyleBox["\"8.34\"", ShowStringCharacters -> False], 8.3375, 
         AutoDelete -> True], NumberForm[#, 3]& ]}, {
      "\"Hooke's law a = -\[Theta]\"", "\"\"", 
       TagBox[
        InterpretationBox[
         StyleBox["\"6.28\"", ShowStringCharacters -> False], 
         6.283333333333334, AutoDelete -> True], NumberForm[#, 3]& ]}, {
      "\"true pendulum a = -sin \[Theta]\"", "\"\"", 
       TagBox[
        InterpretationBox[
         StyleBox["\"8.35\"", ShowStringCharacters -> False], 8.35, 
         AutoDelete -> True], NumberForm[#, 3]& ]}}, 
     GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Left}}}, AutoDelete -> False, 
     GridBoxBackground -> {
      "Columns" -> {{None}}, "RowsIndexed" -> {1 -> GrayLevel[0.92]}}, 
     GridBoxFrame -> {"Columns" -> {{True}}, "Rows" -> {{True}}}, 
     GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}},
      GridBoxSpacings -> {"Columns" -> {{0.8}}, "Rows" -> {{0.5}}}, 
     BaseStyle -> {FontSize -> 10}], "Grid"], 
   StyleBox["\"Table 12\"", Bold, FontSize -> 11, StripOnInput -> False]},
  "Labeled",
  DisplayFunction->(GridBox[{{
      ItemBox[#2, DefaultBaseStyle -> "LabeledLabel"]}, {
      TagBox[
       ItemBox[
        PaneBox[
         TagBox[#, "SkipImageSizeLevel"], Alignment -> {Center, Baseline}, 
         BaselinePosition -> Baseline], DefaultBaseStyle -> "Labeled"], 
       "SkipImageSizeLevel"]}}, 
    GridBoxAlignment -> {"Columns" -> {{Center}}, "Rows" -> {{Center}}}, 
    AutoDelete -> False, 
    GridBoxItemSize -> {"Columns" -> {{Automatic}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
    BaselinePosition -> {2, 1}]& ),
  InterpretationFunction->(RowBox[{"Labeled", "[", 
     RowBox[{#, ",", #2, ",", "Top", ",", 
       RowBox[{"{", "}"}]}], "]"}]& )]], "Output",ExpressionUUID->"7693be6c-\
99d8-48d3-b9d0-9b2643111b87"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell["\<\
Diagram 5. The trained pendulum model, angle in and acceleration out. Six \
\[Sigma] neurons, added up, make the curve -sin \[Theta] of Figure 9.\
\>", "Caption",
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"b38e50df-6cfa-49b6-9d63-d4fcaa248e18"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["\<\
(*c.22b*)
(* the trained force-law network: angle in, acceleration out *)
figure[{{netDiagram[{1, 6, 1}, histP[[-1, 3]], {\"\[Theta]\"}, {\"a(\[Theta])\
\"}, \"\[CapitalSigma]\",
     \"\"]}}, \"Diagram 5. The 1-6-1 pendulum model after training\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"91944ec6-593c-44f2-83f8-8610586d9500"],

