Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Appendix A. The formulas in one place", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"16efab7c-842a-4f10-96cb-515d271291ef"],

Cell["\<\
One neuron: z = w\[CenterDot]x + b, a = \[Sigma](z), Eqs. (1)\[Dash](2); \
\[Sigma]\[Prime] = \[Sigma](1 - \[Sigma]), Eq. (3).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"3179bb92-46e0-4ebe-9891-7622b3b77adc"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A layer: z = W x + b with W of size m \[Times] n (outputs \[Times] inputs), \
Eq. (4); for M samples as rows, Z = X ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["W", "T"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3abdfdfa-e1dc-4984-b83d-a8ceca4f3a7e"],
 " + b, Eq. (5)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"de2e3eb3-0933-4d88-a11f-89bd4b3c0619"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A network: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["a", "0"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "558182b9-6202-412b-a953-72e878fded2e"],
 " = x; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["z", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "26e0eb2b-43ea-4965-828d-e6c8c402ae96"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["W", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "62dcd58f-b069-450a-b8b8-18a0f89fbe77"],
 " times the activations of the previous layer, plus ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["b", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "6f6652cf-48da-48de-a173-1a0568d45665"],
 "; ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["a", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "8189914b-f142-4e02-996b-f3638a0614ae"],
 " = \[Sigma](",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["z", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c3f823bf-3de4-4d60-9621-4a1744a04bb6"],
 "), Eq. (6)."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"bb646efc-7b11-4c45-aa50-6cdc133ed3ed"],

Cell["\<\
Losses: squared error, Eq. (8); softmax and cross-entropy, Eqs. \
(9)\[Dash](10).\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"5d595ed0-5a94-43d6-ae0b-10b448f07d36"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Backpropagation: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "L"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c820342f-43e3-4265-8ce3-faeea5a2199c"],
 " from Eq. (11), ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "64593b83-44ef-4e24-8280-6af271184821"],
 " from Eq. (12), gradients from Eq. (13); the gradient of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["W", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "fc233526-2675-411f-8785-fad5f60252a8"],
 " has the shape of ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["W", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c954be0a-b74e-41fa-bdae-f341a1411176"],
 "."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"09222e6f-2452-4bdb-a44a-f7604c872706"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Training: ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["W", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "3eb4833f-1ce4-406f-98da-a2548134457e"],
 " \[LeftArrow] ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["W", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "58c1669c-92ad-413f-8a15-2c3334d424ea"],
 " - \[Eta] \[PartialD]L/\[PartialD]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["W", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "e62e7207-47ff-4b1a-9d85-0a3ccfc6ca7e"],
 ", Eq. (14); one epoch is one pass over the data; Adam, Eq. (19), adapts the \
step for each weight."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"b85fbf36-de50-4d81-b36c-a45c1cdee0e5"],

Cell["\<\
Learning dynamics: a network can learn what to do (a controller, Section 8) \
or how a system moves (a model, Section 9); a model of the force that depends \
on the position alone conserves energy, Theorem 4.\
\>", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"26809845-5ee3-4da0-bed7-a26ef8266088"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Shapes in the code: X is M \[Times] n, every ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["A", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "c704c90d-865b-45ee-9d16-927bb1427690"],
 " is M \[Times] (neurons of layer l), every \[Delta] is M \[Times] (neurons \
of its layer), and \[PartialD]L/\[PartialD]",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["W", "l"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "7597dfdc-b52c-4a9b-a2e9-a4f96a1d7673"],
 " is ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   SuperscriptBox["\[Delta]", "T"], TraditionalForm]],ExpressionUUID->
  "70bbe891-e2ff-4326-b164-86830da61f2d"],
 " A of the previous layer."
}], "Item",ExpressionUUID->"7d08ca8e-5289-4381-a6f3-4ea46a42673d"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["Appendix B. Saving the animations as videos", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"4a34987f-6fea-47b6-90ca-9cf8c50ebc83"],

Cell["\<\
Every animation in this notebook is a list of frames, and Export turns a list \
of frames into a video. Cells c.0.4, c.14, c.20, c.21 and c.23 keep their \
frames, or a function that draws frame k, under a name: stepView, xorFrames, \
cpView, pushFrames and pendView. Cell c.26 exports five MP4 files into the \
folder of the notebook: the 13 steps of Figure 0.1, the XOR training of \
Figure 5, the push test of Figure 8, the cart-pole at four stages of training \
(Figure 7) and the trained pendulum model (Figure 9). It needs the whole \
notebook to have been run first, and drawing several hundred frames takes a \
few minutes; videos can be switched off one by one in doExport.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"635090f6-e1b0-40c3-8280-2830dfa4a6b1"],

Cell["\<\
The same idea works for any Manipulate: write its body as a function of the \
control variables, as in c.20 and c.23, then Export a Table of that function \
over the values to be shown.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"506f906e-7e21-4077-aede-baa823269531"],

Cell["Table 15. The exported videos and their sizes.", "Caption",
 FontFamily->"Source Sans Pro",
 FontSize->14,ExpressionUUID->"2c33c2a3-19e7-4438-bc36-c5119ebf89eb"],

Cell["\<\
(*c.26*)
(* save the animations as MP4 videos in the notebook's folder. Run the
   notebook first (c.0 to c.25). Export draws every frame, so this
   takes a few minutes; set doExport to False to skip a video *)
dir = If[StringQ[Quiet@NotebookDirectory[]], NotebookDirectory[],
   $HomeDirectory];
video[name_, frames_, fps_] := Export[FileNameJoin[{dir, name}],
   frames, \"MP4\", \"FrameRate\" -> fps];
doExport = <|\"steps\" -> True, \"xor\" -> True, \"push\" -> True,
   \"balance\" -> True, \"pendulum\" -> True|>;
files = DeleteCases[{
   If[doExport[\"steps\"], video[\"Tiny-network-13-steps.mp4\",
     Table[stepView[k], {k, Length[allSteps]}], 1]],
   If[doExport[\"xor\"], video[\"XOR-training.mp4\", xorFrames, 8]],
   If[doExport[\"push\"], video[\"CartPole-push-test.mp4\", pushFrames,
     25]],
   (* Figure 7 at four training snapshots, 6 s each *)
   If[doExport[\"balance\"], video[\"CartPole-learning.mp4\", Flatten@Table[
       cpView[j, n], {j, {1, 3, 5, Length[pick]}}, {n, 1, 301, 3}],
     17]],
   (* Figure 9 for the trained model: 40 time units *)
   If[doExport[\"pendulum\"], video[\"Pendulum-learned.mp4\",
     Table[pendView[Length[pickP], n], {n, 1, 801, 4}], 20]]},
  Null];
table[Prepend[{FileNameTake[#], Round[FileByteCount[#]/1024.], \" kB\"} & /@
    files, {\"video\", \"size\", \"\"}], \"Table 15. The exported videos\"]\
\>", "Input",ExpressionUUID->"23a1f099-74de-48e4-99e4-d1c34bb0e1f5"]
}, Open  ]],

